cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ALAKAZAM: ALuminium Ablation Kinetics And Z-resolved Atmospheric injection Model"
type: software
abstract: >-
  ALAKAZAM is a re-entry and ablation model that estimates how much aluminium
  a satellite evaporates during atmospheric entry and at which altitudes it is
  injected into the mesosphere, with boiling at the local stagnation pressure,
  temperature-dependent emissivity of oxidised and bare aluminium, and
  automated checks that keep the reported numbers in sync with the code.
